esce and again we  can look at the reconstruction of that  which does a little dance for us so we  can do a certain amount of animation to  show the potential movement in the  little fossil so again this is a  remarkable preservation and then finally  the importance of fantastic fossils they  increase our knowledge of extinct  creatures that we simply would know  nothing about the easiest easiest  example is if we had no fossil record  we'd have no idea there had ever been  dinosaurs but I've shown you other kinds  of animals that tell you the same story  they show you the evolutionary history  that leads to life today and of course  as we've seen they reveal the nature of  ancient communities  and of course my final message is that  at the Peabody Museum every day he is a  and you can work that out for yourselves  and then I'm going to insert a little  video that will show you a little bit  more about that  extraordinary animal OPA binya and let  me see if I can get that to behave now  okay yes you can abort
 

